@meeting introBriefing
// Day 1, Monday 07:50, the Works bay: Calder's Monday briefing, Torres and two Works crew on shift (cast 'works:2':
// the script's tech1 and tech2). The Works writer; head writer 5 (0.48.76, the user's note): Torres shadows you, three
// practical tips, and all that goes on aboard outside work (never called "traditions"). One choice, no wrong answer.
title: Monday briefing
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: The Monday briefing: Calder put you with Torres for the day, gave three rules for the bay, and told you to join in aboard.
== lines
calder: Ten to eight. Good. Everyone's here.   [nod]
calder: Board's at twelve. Two scrubbers, a lamp on Deck 4, the dish pit. A usual Monday.
calder > you: {me}. Arrived last night. Works, from today.
tech1 > you: Morning, new hand.   [gesture]
tech2 > you: Welcome to Works. Tea's at half ten. That's the important bit.
calder: Torres. One job, end to end. Board to turn-in. Their hands, not yours.
torres-zeke: Their hands. Got it, Chief.
calder > you: Torres shadows you today. Every step. He'll talk you through it. He talks a lot. Listen anyway.
torres-zeke: I do talk a lot. It's mostly useful.   [laugh]
calder > you: Three things. Gloves on before the panel comes off. Not after.
calder > you: If you don't know, ask. Asking takes a minute. Guessing takes a shift.
calder > you: And put tools back where you found them. The wall has outlines. Use them.
tech2: She means it about the wall.   [gesture]
calder > you: Last thing. Work ends at five. The ship doesn't.
calder > you: Sunday dinner at the long tables. Music on Fridays. Quiz nights. Observatory nights.
calder > you: The garden, the lounge. Knitters, rowers, whoever's learning the guitar this month. Find your lot.
calder > you: People who join in settle in. I've watched it for years. Go to things.
? choice
* Ready when you are.   rel:torres-zeke+1 flavour:cheer
  torres-zeke: That's the spirit. Right, onward.   [laugh]
* What if I get something wrong?   rel:calder+1 flavour:listen
  calder: Then you say so, and we fix it. That's the job.
* (Nod)
  calder: Good. Quiet's fine.
calder: Right. Board's there. Back to it.
